  "notes": "Drawn from 747-8Fs LX-VCA (2025) and LX-VCD (2024). Freighters have no windows. Individual 747s carry city names and sponsor badges by the door (e.g. 'City of Luxembourg'), not drawn. The 747-400Fs wear the same scheme. LX-VCC wears a 50th anniversary scheme and LX-VCM a 'cutaway' special (not this). Re-checked 2026-11-15 on LX-VCJ (747-8F, left, 2026-10-30): 'cargolux' starts at x 0.143 just behind the forward door (not 0.124) and runs 0.211; its ascenders reach ~0.28 r above the red stripe's top, so its height is 0.5 (from 0.6), its lowercase 0.8 of the ascenders; the stripes start right behind its x (0.355, from 0.33). The small 'cargolux' by the nose cube is too small on any photo to measure a length: left without one.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). Cargolux has flown the red tail with the cube mark and red over blue stripes since the 1980s, refreshed with lower-case titles."
}
